# --- D-WORLD-20 APPLIED 2026-08-19 (Mark, attended, #68: "Remove deepseek flash") ---
# The ratified chain becomes codex -> opus. This SUPERSEDES the middle link of
# D-WORLD-ROUTE-1 ("DeepSeek v4 Flash second") and nothing else in it.
#
# WHY HERE AND NOT IN THE DRIVER: tools/launchd/* is FROZEN CORE (D-WORLD-DRIVER-1), and
# mission-control.sh:331 defaults the tail with
#   export MISSION_EXECUTOR_FALLBACK="${MISSION_EXECUTOR_FALLBACK:-pi:openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash-0731:floor}"
# This file is sourced at line 58-59, i.e. BEFORE 331, so a value set here wins the
# ${VAR:-default} and the pi link is never reachable. Same lever, same precedent as the
# iter-23 PATH fix and the retired chain block above.
#
# EVIDENCE FOR THE SUSPENSION (>= 3 datapoints, the charter's routing-change bar, MET):
# five consecutive pi:deepseek executor runs changed ZERO useful bytes across FOUR distinct
# mechanisms (iters 91 x2 stopReason=stop at 625 tok; 92 thinking_delta 325 MB; 93/94 size
# ceiling at ~330 MB with stopReason="length" count 0). The skill's prescribed stopReason
# detector fired on 0 of 5; only a file-SIZE poll ever fired. See memory
# pi-deepseek-lane-4-for-4-dead and charter queue notes.
#
# --- D-WORLD-20 LIFTED 2026-08-26 (Mark, attended). RE-QUALIFICATION RATIFIED. ---
# The suspension above stands as an accurate record of what was OBSERVED. It is lifted
# because the CAUSE was found, and it was ours, not the model's.
#
# Read from the provider's own side of the wire (OpenRouter Broadcast traces, now ingested
# into the prod observatory), all five failures are one mechanism: the model streamed ONLY
# reasoning tokens and emitted no content or tool call. Across the whole 08-18..08-22 corpus,
# 3 of 173 generations had no finish_reason; ALL THREE had completion:"" with
# output_tokens == reasoning_tokens. The other 170 carried content or tool_calls.
#
# The runs did not die on their own — the file-SIZE poll killed them, and it was measuring an
# artefact. pi's message_update replays the WHOLE accumulated message per delta (pi 0.73.1,
# dist/core/agent-session.js:421-427), so NDJSON bytes are QUADRATIC in emitted tokens:
# 7,130 reasoning tokens produced 330 MB. At the declared 65,536-token budget that is ~28 GB,
# i.e. the size ceiling capped this lane at ~7,000 reasoning tokens by accident. That is also
# why the two prompt-level anti-runaway fixes (iters 172, 173) changed nothing — they were
# aimed at a model problem that did not exist.
#
# Nor is it deepseek-specific: the same signature fired on z-ai/glm-5.2 under OpenCode.
#
# WHAT CHANGED SO THIS IS NOT A REPEAT: the lane now runs through scripts/mission_pi_run.sh,
# which filters message_update out of the banked NDJSON (size becomes linear), keeps a bounded
# snapshot for forensics, and emits a TYPED verdict — separating reasoning_stall from
# stream_dead from empty_worktree instead of returning rc=0 for all three.
#
# POSTURE: fallback link only, NOT a rotation peer. Promotion is earned on runs, not on this
# fix — see the PROMOTION RULE in .claude/skills/mission-control/SKILL.md (two consecutive
# `ok` verdicts with a non-empty worktree diff; any non-zero verdict resets the count).
#
# ROLLBACK: uncomment the opus line to re-apply the suspension. No driver edit needed —
# tools/launchd/* stays frozen core (D-WORLD-DRIVER-1); this file is sourced before the
# driver's ${VAR:-default}, so whatever is set here wins.
# MISSION_EXECUTOR_FALLBACK="${MISSION_EXECUTOR_FALLBACK:-opus}"
#
# Unset here = the driver's own default chain applies: codex -> pi:deepseek -> opus.
# Deliberately the UNFLOORED id: :floor is provider.sort=price, which routed every run to the
# two least-healthy hosts by construction (StreamLake -2, Decart -5). Dropped in fc6e42682.
